<!--
    The IEEE 14-bus test system with a meshed multi-terminal DC grid: complements ieee14-dc.xiidm (Ieee14DcNetwork.create, flat).

    The machines Dynawo's IEEE 14-bus test case's (MPL-2.0, nrt/data/IEEE14, its parameter sets 2 to 6): G1, G2 and G3 of four
    windings, G6 and G8 of three - their missing slow q winding one of 0.99 Xq and a T'q0 ten times their T''q0, all but absent -, each
    on its own rating (1211, 1120, 1650, 80 and 250 MVA), its saturation Dynawo's md * psi^nd as S(1.0) = md, S(1.2) = md 1.2^nd; its
    voltage regulator Dynawo's proportional one, a gain of 20 on the voltage error within +-5 pu of field voltage (a 1 ms lag the
    model needs), no stabilizer (a PSS1A switched off, the pipeline's default otherwise); G1 and G2 on Dynawo's proportional
    governor, KGover 5 on their turbines' 1090 and 1008 MW, the synchronous condensers G3, G6 and G8 with none. Dynawo's step-up
    transformers, inside its machines, left out: the machines on their buses, as the case has them.

    The DC grid's converters averaged as CIGRE DCS2's, a 15 % phase reactor on their rating (R 0.003 pu), DC capacitors of 40 ms, a
    bridge inductance for their blocking: CS2, CS3 and CS9 grid-following (on their DC voltage or droop, as IIDM's control mode says),
    CSW grid-forming (a virtual synchronous machine), its island's. The wind park WTW Dynawo's WT4B example
    (ExampleNetworks.wt4bDynawoExample) on its own 150 MVA. Each DC line one lumped pi of its 400 kV conductor: 2 L and C / 2 of CIGRE
    B4's +-200 kV per-km pole data (OHL 0.8273 mH, 0.0139 uF; cable 2.615 mH, 0.2185 uF).
-->
